# local/ lab conventions

**New operator / AI agent:** follow the **Agent playbook** in repo root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (section *Agent playbook — run the local lab on the operator's stack*) before running commands. Never assume a specific Grafana Cloud stack; always use the operator's `GC_OTLP_*` in `local/.env`.

## Topology

1 spine + 2 leaves + 2 clients (`ixrd2l`). Configs in `local/configs/fabric/`. Lab name `srl-local`; Docker mgmt network **`clab`** (`CLAB_NETWORK=clab`).

## Compose (KtransToGrafana golden path)

`compose-base.yaml` + `compose-groups.generated.yaml` + `compose-catalog.generated.yaml` + `compose-limits.generated.yaml` (via `make up`).

Services: `alloy`, `gnmic`, `ktranslate_snmp_srl`, `ktranslate_flow`, `ktranslate_sflow`, `ktranslate_syslog`. Optional: `topology_exporter` (compose profile `topology`, `LAB_TOPOLOGY_EXPORTER=1`).

- Groups: `groups/srl.env` → `make generate` → poller/discovery configs under `config/` + `state/`
- Discovery: `make snmp-discover` (CIDR sync + discover all groups) or `make discover GROUP=srl` — not `--snmp_discovery_on_start`
- SNMP profiles: bundled in the ktranslate image; discovery assigns `mib_profile` from `sysObjectID` — see [kentik/snmp-profiles](https://github.com/kentik/snmp-profiles) for edge cases
- Alloy: `local/alloy/config.alloy` — comments must be `//` only. Receives OTLP; scrapes Docker logs for Clos + sidecars (skips ktranslate — those use `--tee_logs` OTLP); remaps gnmic LLDP → `network_topology_edge_info`; stamps `deployment.host`
- gnmic: `local/gnmic/gnmic.yaml` (OTLP → Alloy; includes `lldp_neighbors` subscribe)
- topology-exporter (optional): `local/topology-exporter/config.yaml` — `make topology-up` after `topology-exporter-image`
- NetBox Cloud: optional — `scripts/netbox-populate.py` + `make netbox-sync` when `DISCOVERY_SOURCE=netbox` (`groups/srl.env.netbox.sample`); default uses CIDR discovery via `sync-snmp-discovery.sh`

## Scripts

- LF line endings only (CRLF breaks bash under WSL).
- `sync-snmp-discovery.sh` — sync clab mgmt CIDR → `groups/*.env` TARGETS, run discovery, reload collectors (`make snmp-discover`)
- `update-snmp-targets.sh` — clab IPAM subnet → TARGETS + `make generate` (called by sync-snmp-discovery)
- `update-topology-targets.sh` — rewrite topology-exporter `host:` lines + sync `tester_id`
- `netbox-bootstrap.sh` / `make netbox-sync` / `make netbox-sync-mgmt` — populate NetBox Cloud + mgmt IPs for SNMP discovery
- `lab-path.sh` / `sync-clab-workdir.sh` / `clab.sh` — ContainerLab deploy helpers (internal; operators should use a WSL ext4 clone, not `/mnt/c`)
- `apply-fabric-config.sh` / `make fabric-apply` / `make fabric-up` — load `configs/fabric/*.cfg` (default path: SNMP-only via `enable-snmp-srl.sh`; `FULL_FABRIC=1` pipes entire flat cfg — risky on running lab)
- `staggered-up.sh` — default `make up` path: fabric nodes then collectors one-by-one (`LAB_STAGGER_SECS`, logs RAM)
- `stabilize-lab.sh` / `make stabilize` — recover without `clab deploy --reconfigure` (start SRL, apply fabric, discover)
- `snmp-check.sh` / `make snmp-check` — TARGETS vs live clab IPs, snmpget, devices yaml, poller logs, Grafana `kentik_snmp_*` (not `DeviceMetrics`)
- `finish-bringup.sh` / `make snmp-recover` — after clab IP drift: enable SNMP → `sync-snmp-discovery.sh`
- `finish-flows.sh` / `make finish-flows` — EVPN check, softflowd, traffic, verify `network_io_by_flow_bytes` in Grafana
- `lab-log.sh` / `lab-log-status` / `lab-log-events` — audit trail in `state/lab-actions.log` + `docker-events.log` (container die/stop correlation)
- `enable-snmp-srl.sh` — restore SNMP on mgmt NI: delete clab `SNMPv2-RO-Community`, set `ag1` + `community-entry ce1 community public` (used by `fabric-apply` and recovery)
- `restore-mgmt-ni.sh` — recreate `network-instance mgmt` when wiped; then run `enable-snmp-srl.sh`
- `apply-fabric-node.sh` — pipe one node's `configs/fabric/<node>.cfg` (debug/recovery only; prefer `make fabric-apply`)
- `softflowd.sh` — clients → `ktranslate_flow:9995`
- `syslog-config.sh` — `docker exec -i` + `sr_cli` → `ktranslate_syslog:1514` (requires `system logging network-instance mgmt`)
- `snmp-trap-config.sh` — SRL `trap-group ktranslate` via mgmt → **same** `ktranslate_snmp_srl` container UDP `1620` / `public` (not a separate collector)
- `post-telemetry-config.sh` — after discovery: flow-dns, softflowd, sFlow, syslog, traps, mgmt-api-mock, traffic, events-loop (`LAB_AUTO_TRAFFIC` / `LAB_AUTO_EVENTS`)
- `emit-events.sh` — apply syslog+trap config, flap leaf client/spine links for real traps+syslog
- `events-loop.sh` — background traps every 3m + emit-events every 5m (`make events-loop|events-stop|events-status`)
- `traffic.sh` — ongoing client1↔client2 UDP workloads (steady 3M, burst 8M/20s, reverse 1M, ping 1/s); TCP iperf can stall, but short HTTP (join-app) works
- `join-app.sh` — OTel Go HTTP client on client1 → server on client2 (`172.17.0.2:8080`); traces → `alloy:4317`
- `join-fault.sh` — tc netem delay/loss on client eth1 for Investigation talk track
- `trap-gen.sh` — synthetic SNMPv2c traps to poller (`make traps`)

## Operator commands

`make -C local up|up-parallel|down|status|stabilize|fabric-up|fabric-apply|snmp-check|snmp-recover|finish-flows|lab-log-status|traffic|traffic-stop|traffic-status|join-app|join-app-stop|join-app-status|join-fault|join-fault-stop|join-fault-status|events-loop|events-stop|events-status|logs|generate|discover|discover-all|topology-up|topology-exporter-image|topology-targets|netbox-sync|netbox-sync-mgmt` or root `make local-up`. On Windows, agents run via `wsl -e bash -lc 'cd ~/projects/network-o11y-demo/local && …'` (ext4 clone only).

**Agent rule:** never `clab deploy --reconfigure` unless the user explicitly requests it. Use `make stabilize` to recover stopped SRL nodes. On Windows, never run the lab from `/mnt/c` — use a WSL ext4 clone.

**Windows agents:** do not embed `$var` or `for` loops in PowerShell→`wsl` one-liners; call `bash scripts/…` instead. Sync `configs/fabric/` and `scripts/` to `~/network-o11y-demo` after editing on `C:\`. Strip CRLF on new shell scripts before running in WSL.

## Fabric SNMP contract

`configs/fabric/{spine1,leaf1,leaf2}.cfg` must define **`network-instance mgmt`** (`type ip-vrf`, `interface mgmt0.0`, linux protocol) and **`system snmp access-group ag1 community-entry ce1 community public`**. Telemetry (gNMI, SNMP, syslog, traps, sFlow) binds to **mgmt** — if mgmt NI or SNMP community is missing, ktranslate logs show `connection refused` on :161 even when containers are up.

## Topology metrics

- Devices: `network_topology_device_info` (optional topology_exporter; `tester_id` from `LAB_TESTER_ID`)
- Edges: `network_topology_edge_info` (gnmic LLDP YANG → Alloy remap; stock SRL SNMP has no LLDP rem-table)

